no_prelude

# `argv_get_bytes` is the ONE capability this design deliberately removes
# (docs/no-prelude-core-v0.md §8), and it is pinned here so the removal cannot be
# undone by accident.
#
# It leaves because its signature is `Int -> Maybe Bytes !{IO}` and `Maybe` is a
# prelude-declared type. Admitting it would mean admitting `Maybe` to the floor, and a
# floor carrying a prelude ADT lands a `Maybe` in the namespace of exactly the files most
# likely to declare their own — which re-triggers both open qualification-uniformity bugs
# (`__cm_<Class>_<method>` mangling and do-notation's bare-name monad lookup).
#
# That is not a trade worth making for one name: reading argv from a file that
# has opted out of the standard library is a thin use case, and nothing in the
# repo does it.

fn main() -> Int !{IO} =
  match argv_get_bytes(0) with
  | Just _ -> 1
  | Nothing -> 0
